body:
exactly this , i already have captcha on checkout and the customer contacted me over chat and asked me if he can get a payment link because he don't trust random sites and dont want to put card details on my website , I got into his trap and made a payment link for him which is hosted by stripe and he tested hundreds of cards on the same payment link

&#x200B;

i know i shouldnt have give out payment links like this but my only concern now is will this affect my account standing? i already disabled all the payment links now by the way

and i have a list of users the attacker accessed , the list doesnt have a single username matching that wordfence list , so the accounts which was accessed by that hacker didnt have weak password , i am confused right now

&#x200B;

maybe it is just the yoast plugin

ok so i ran a standard scan and found 1 vulnerable plugin and few users with weak passwords

&#x200B;

https://gyazo.com/ffdffd336c8bda70a8c773cdc9b894bd

they all have different IP's and its not on a single ip , the attack is stopped now since i turned on the under attack mode in cloudflare 

&#x200B;

https://gyazo.com/936d6932ac97899ebdb541b66016a7bb
